//? Title: Seeed DevArm CAD workflow
//? Subtitle: Download, import, pose, export and render in C++, Python and R
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

> Seeed DevArm: download, import, pose, export and visualize

Each tab below is one complete workflow. Run it from this document's directory:
it obtains the pinned source files through `datasets::fetch`, imports the real
arm and a precise STEP link, poses the arm, exports both models as glTF,
reopens those exports and renders them here. No separate `just cad-assets`
step or downloader script is needed.
Python and R use the native packages built with `just build-python` and
`just build-r`.

The input is [Seeed reBot-DevArm|https://github.com/Seeed-Projects/reBot-DevArm]
B601-DM, pinned to revision `922c5fa3d8c8919db1847b49166f02fc26c8fdad`.
The native downloader verifies all 38 files by size and SHA-256, including
the source license, URDF, 34 visual STL meshes and STEP geometry (about 56 MB).
The explicit cache below is the repository's ignored `build/cad-assets/rebot`;
omitting the second fetch argument uses the shared configurable dataset cache.
A valid cache works offline; set `DATAMUNGE_DATA_OFFLINE=1` to forbid downloads.
A changed cached file raises an error. `DATAMUNGE_DATA_MIRROR` can supply a
mirror laid out as `rebot_devarm/<file basename>`.

The arm has seven independent joints. Angles are radians and the gripper
coordinate is metres; its right finger follows the URDF mimic relation.
The STEP link uses millimetres, so it stays in a separate scene. Exported glTF
stores the posed render meshes, placements and colors; keep the URDF to change
joints and the STEP source for exact B-rep surfaces. Exporting glTF does not
preserve joint constraints or the STEP feature representation. The programs
check that the reopened exports retain every object and triangle before
rendering them. This example visualizes geometry without commanding hardware.

The source hardware is © 2026 Seeed Studio Co., Ltd., CERN-OHL-W-2.0.
The downloaded `LICENSE` remains beside the assets. Cached images are included
in this report for viewing before running the code. Newly generated PNGs and
self-contained glTF files stay in this report's local `build/` directory;
no image XML, data URIs or model bytes are printed into the results.

\tabs(

\tab(C++,

```{cpp, results="markdown", nix-shell="git+file:../../../..#cpp", cmd="c++ -std=c++23 -O2 {file} -o {bin} $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge) && {bin}", file="figures/rebot_arm.png"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <filesystem>
#include <print>
#include <stdexcept>

int main() {
  // Download missing source files and verify the complete cache on every run.
  const std::filesystem::path assets = dm::datasets::fetch(
    "rebot_devarm", "../../../../build/cad-assets/rebot");
  const std::filesystem::path out = "build/cad_cpp";
  std::filesystem::create_directories(out);
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build/figs");

  auto arm = dm::cad::View::from_urdf(
    (assets / "Rebot_Arm_description/DM/urdf/ReBot_Arm_DM.urdf").string());
  arm.set_joint("joint2", -.8);
  arm.set_joint("joint3", -.7);
  arm.set_joint("finger_left", .015); // The right finger follows automatically.
  arm.save_gltf((out / "rebot_arm.gltf").string());

  auto part = dm::cad::View::from_file(
    (assets / "hardware/reBot_B601_DM/Metal_Parts/03_Link1.step").string());
  part.save_gltf((out / "rebot_link1.gltf").string());

  // Import the saved models: the displayed images visualize these exports.
  auto saved_arm = dm::cad::View::from_file((out / "rebot_arm.gltf").string());
  auto saved_part = dm::cad::View::from_file((out / "rebot_link1.gltf").string());
  if (saved_arm.object_count() != arm.object_count() ||
      saved_arm.triangle_count() != arm.triangle_count() ||
      saved_part.object_count() != part.object_count() ||
      saved_part.triangle_count() != part.triangle_count())
    throw std::runtime_error("Export changed the object or triangle count");

  saved_part.size(900, 650);
  saved_part.samples(2);
  saved_part.light(.5, -1, 2, "#ffffff", 1.2);
  saved_part.light(-1, .5, .5, "#dce8ff", .5);
  saved_part.render("build/figs/rebot_link1.png");
  std::filesystem::create_directories("figures");
  std::filesystem::copy_file("build/figs/rebot_link1.png", "figures/rebot_link1.png",
    std::filesystem::copy_options::overwrite_existing);
  saved_arm.size(1100, 850);
  saved_arm.samples(2);
  saved_arm.light(.5, -1, 2, "#ffffff", 1.3);
  saved_arm.light(-1, -.5, .5, "#dce8ff", .6);
  saved_arm.render("build/figs/rebot_arm.png");

  std::println("| Source | Objects | Triangles | Reopened objects | Reopened triangles |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |");
  std::println("| Posed DevArm | {} | {} | {} | {} |", arm.object_count(),
    arm.triangle_count(), saved_arm.object_count(), saved_arm.triangle_count());
  std::println("| STEP link | {} | {} | {} | {} |", part.object_count(),
    part.triangle_count(), saved_part.object_count(), saved_part.triangle_count());
}
```
